Recompiler: bltzall and bgezall write the link register whether or not the branch is taken.

What it fixes: ControlFlowEmitter::emitConditionalBranch wrote $ra only inside the taken path for the
"branch likely and link" forms (BLTZALL, BGEZALL). The reference emulator's interpreter
(third_party/pcsx2/pcsx2/Interpreter.cpp, Interpreter::OpcodeImpl::BLTZALL / BGEZALL) executes
_SetLink(31) first, as for BLTZAL / BGEZAL, so $ra = branch address + 8 in both outcomes. Found by
tests/conformance (family "branches"): bltzall failed 18 of 26 cases and bgezall 8 of 26, always the
not-taken ones ($ra kept its old value). The census (docs/knowledge/data/instruction_conformance.tsv)
gives the number of bltzall / bgezall sites in the game.

How it was verified: the conformance tests of branches pass with a recompiler relinked with this change
and fail without it (the pytest command of tests/conformance, see journal 025).

Original work for this repository (no code from another project).

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
index 95f69d7..56b5904 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
@@ -468,14 +468,11 @@ namespace ps2recomp
 
         if (m_branchInst.opcode == OPCODE_REGIMM)
         {
-            if (m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BLTZAL || m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BGEZAL)
+            if (m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BLTZAL || m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BGEZAL ||
+                m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BLTZALL || m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BGEZALL)
             {
                 unconditionalLinkCode = fmt::format("SET_GPR_U32(ctx, 31, 0x{:X}u);", fallthroughPc());
             }
-            else if (m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BLTZALL || m_branchInst.rt == REGIMM_BGEZALL)
-            {
-                conditionalLinkCode = fmt::format("SET_GPR_U32(ctx, 31, 0x{:X}u);", fallthroughPc());
-            }
         }
 
         m_ss << "    {\n";
